): Affirmed Parliament's power to amend fundamental rights. 25th Amendment (1971): Article 31C protecting DPSP laws from fundamental rights challenge.

Major Constitutional Amendments - 42nd to 44th 42nd Amendment (1976): Added Fundamental Duties, made DPSP override fundamental rights, curtailed judicial review. 44th Amendment (1978): Restored judicial review, removed right to property from fundamental rights (made Article 300A), modified emergency provisions, protected media freedom.

Major Constitutional Amendments - 52nd to 101st 52nd Amendment (1985): Anti-defection law (Tenth Schedule). 73rd & 74th (1992): Panchayats and Municipalities. 86th (2002): Right to Education (Article 21A). 97th (2011): Co-operative societies. 101st (2016): Goods and Services Tax (GST). 103rd (2019): EWS reservation. 105th (2021): Restored states' power to identify OBCs.

